{
  "question": "QL on Ozempic pens?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming NY Medicaid (coverage/QL question, no program named).",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: the NYRx PDL (revised 9/14/2026) lists **no quantity limit** for Ozempic pens.\n\n- Ozempic pen is in the GLP-1 RA (Type 2 DM) class, listed as preferred (the PDL's preferred/non-preferred status is marked \"as of 10/22/2026\", which is not yet in effect as of today, 10/14/2026).\n- The class has clinical criteria (CC) only: confirm a FDA-approved/compendia-supported and Medicaid-covered indication, and PA is required if the patient is on a GLP-1 plus a DPP-IV concurrently.\n- The only GLP-1-type lifetime QLs on the PDL are for Wegovy and Zepbound (two treatment attempts per lifetime).\n- Any plan-level pen-count or days-supply limit isn't in these documents.",
